    "postMarkdown": "Five years ago, a 20kW rack was considered high density. In 2026, 40kW to 100kW per rack is the baseline standard for AI factories.\n\nPacking 100kW into a standard 42U footprint requires solving three simultaneous physical challenges: heavy structural floor loading, high-voltage busway distribution, and continuous hydronic cooling loops.\n\n1. Structural Weight Dynamics: Liquid-filled chassis and heavy copper heatsinks pushing rack weights past 3,000 lbs.\n\n2. Power Distribution Transition: Migrating from 208V AC to 415V/480V busbars and 48V DC power shelves to eliminate rectifier losses.\n\n3. Hydronic Loop Redundancy: Dual-loop CDUs (Coolant Distribution Units) ensuring zero disruption during thermal pump maintenance.\n\n4. Facility Footprint Optimization: Achieving 5x compute capacity within existing building envelopes.\n\nThe future of AI is physical. The companies that master thermal and electrical density will lead the intelligence economy.\n\n---\n→ Discuss High-Density Facility Engineering with TrustGrid: https://trustgrid.ai\n\n#HighDensityCompute #AIInfrastructure #DataCenter #CleanTech #TrustGrid\n",
