    "postMarkdown": "If your AI dashboard still tracks 'CPU Load' and 'RAM Usage,' you are flying blind into an infrastructure storm.\n\nTraditional observability tools were designed for stateless microservices. Production AI infrastructure requires metrics rooted in tensor math, memory bandwidth, and token economics.\n\n1. 1. Model FLOPs Utilization (MFU): The percentage of peak theoretical tensor operations actually executing useful calculations.\n\n2. 2. Time-to-First-Token (TTFT) p99: The true metric of responsiveness for interactive users and autonomous agent loops.\n\n3. 3. All-Reduce Synchronization Wait Time: The percentage of GPU time spent stalled waiting on inter-node network communication.\n\n4. 4. Cost per 1M Validated Tokens: The ultimate financial attribution metric connecting silicon burn to enterprise value.\n\nYou cannot optimize what you do not accurately measure. Upgrade your telemetry to reflect the physics of AI.\n\n---\n→ Download TrustGrid's Enterprise AI Telemetry & Metrics Standard: https://trustgrid.ai\n\n#AIMetrics #Observability #PlatformEngineering #AILeadership #TrustGrid\n",
