    "postMarkdown": "When a human employee is compromised, damage is limited by human typing speed. When an autonomous agent is compromised, damage happens at machine speed.\n\nAutonomous systems can execute thousands of transactions per minute across enterprise databases, cloud infrastructure, and financial ledgers.\n\n1. 1. Cascading Blast Radius: A poisoned agent propagating corrupt data across multiple downstream enterprise systems before security teams detect the anomaly.\n\n2. 2. Autonomous Deadlocks & Infinite Tool Loops: Malicious inputs designed to trap agents in recursive API execution loops, running up tens of thousands in compute bills.\n\n3. 3. Attacking the Agent Communication Fabric: Man-in-the-middle attacks injecting falsified messages into inter-agent communication channels.\n\n4. 4. Deterministic Circuit Breakers: Real-time anomaly monitors that freeze agent permissions within 100 milliseconds of detecting unexpected transaction spikes.\n\nSpeed is the superpower of autonomous systems. It must be balanced with automated, millisecond-level defensive circuit breakers.\n\n---\n→ Schedule an Autonomous Systems Security Briefing: https://trustgrid.ai\n\n#AutonomousSecurity #CyberRisk #AgenticAI #EnterpriseGovernance #TrustGrid\n",
