    "postMarkdown": "When Shor's algorithm runs on a quantum computer, every RSA-2048 key on Earth will be broken in minutes.\n\nModern digital commerce, VPN tunnels, TLS certificates, and API tokens rely on mathematical problems that quantum computers solve effortlessly.\n\n1. Building a Cryptographic Bill of Materials (CBOM): Discovering every legacy algorithm, key size, and certificate authority across your enterprise IT estate.\n\n2. Transitioning to NIST Post-Quantum Standards: Implementing lattice-based algorithms like ML-KEM (Kyber) for key encapsulation and ML-DSA (Dilithium) for digital signatures.\n\n3. Hybrid Classical-Quantum Deployments: Running dual classical + post-quantum cryptographic layers to maintain current FIPS compliance while future-proofing against quantum decryption.\n\n4. Network Protocol Upgrades: Updating TLS 1.3 handshakes, SSH tunnels, and VPN configurations to handle larger post-quantum key and signature sizes.\n\nThe transition to post-quantum cryptography is the largest cryptographic migration in human history. Preparation begins with your CBOM.\n\n---\n→ Download TrustGrid's Post-Quantum Readiness Roadmap: https://trustgrid.ai\n\n#PostQuantum #PQC #Cryptography #CyberDefense #TrustGrid\n",
