    "postMarkdown": "Quantum-safe defense does not require buying a quantum computer. It requires upgrading your math.\n\nThere is widespread executive confusion between Quantum Computing (hardware that performs quantum math) and Quantum-Safe Cryptography (classical algorithms mathematically resistant to quantum attacks).\n\n1. The Foundation of Quantum-Safe Defense: Mathematical hardness assumptions based on high-dimensional lattice problems that are intractable for both classical and quantum computers.\n\n2. Post-Quantum Algorithms (PQC): Software-deployable algorithms running on standard enterprise servers, CPUs, and mobile devices without specialized quantum hardware.\n\n3. Crypto-Agility Architecture: Designing modular security layers where encryption algorithms can be swapped via configuration without recompiling core enterprise software.\n\n4. Defense-in-Depth Integration: Combining PQC with hardware roots of trust, zero-trust network boundaries, and continuous memory attestation.\n\nQuantum-safe defense is practical, mathematically proven, and deployable on existing enterprise hardware today.\n\n---\n→ Review TrustGrid's Quantum-Safe Defense Architecture: https://trustgrid.ai\n\n#QuantumSafe #CyberDefense #EnterpriseSecurity #PQC #TrustGrid\n",
