    "postMarkdown": "Trust is not a feeling. In enterprise autonomous systems, trust is a set of hard mathematical and architectural guarantees.\n\nAutonomous systems must operate within strict parameter spaces. Trust Engineering is the discipline of enforcing those boundaries programmatically.\n\n1. Input Boundary Verification: Validating schemas, token lengths, and semantic bounds before prompts ever touch model inference engines.\n\n2. Deterministic Tool Interception: Validating API payloads and database queries against formal schema constraints prior to execution.\n\n3. Output Grounding & Factuality Checks: Using secondary verification models to verify that generated assertions are 100% grounded in retrieved reference facts.\n\n4. Automated Rollback & Circuit Breakers: Automatically freezing agent execution and reverting system mutations if anomaly thresholds are exceeded.\n\nEngineer trust directly into your runtime architecture. It is the only way to deploy autonomous systems with absolute confidence.\n\n---\n→ Explore TrustGrid's Trust Engineering Architecture Blueprint: https://trustgrid.ai\n\n#TrustEngineering #AutonomousSystems #SystemDesign #Reliability #TrustGrid\n",
